77
00:04:37,867 --> 00:04:43,604
The Pod names carry the ReplicaSet's name, which carries a hash of the template.

78
00:04:43,604 --> 00:04:43,748
3.

79
00:04:43,748 --> 00:04:50,346
Ask the application which version it is (through port-forward to the Deployment, lesson 04):

80
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:55,010
How do I see what Kubernetes did?

81
00:04:55,567 --> 00:04:57,326
Ask the cluster.

82
00:04:59,067 --> 00:05:00,967
Let me try something.

83
00:05:00,967 --> 00:05:08,026
A release with a typo in the image tag, 9.9.9, a version that was never built:

84
00:05:08,567 --> 00:05:10,270
What should happen?

85
00:05:10,270 --> 00:05:12,960
Three Pods on the new version.

86
00:05:12,960 --> 00:05:14,215
What happened?

87
00:05:14,215 --> 00:05:16,636
The rollout never finishes.

88
00:05:18,400 --> 00:05:21,089
Roll back to the previous revision:

89
00:05:22,833 --> 00:05:23,547
Got it.

90
00:05:23,547 --> 00:05:26,298
What do I need to remember?

91
00:05:26,833 --> 00:05:33,443
Deployment → ReplicaSets → Pods; a template change creates a new ReplicaSet and a rolling update.

92
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:40,479
maxSurge and maxUnavailable control the pace; readiness decides when a new Pod counts.

93
00:05:41,033 --> 00:05:47,318
rollout status, rollout history, rollout undo watch, explain and revert.
